  "body": "Asked for by the maintainer (2026-11-13, in chat, after the v0.19.0 cut): \"We should as a rule not let P1/P2s coming in after cut - force a restart as its a ~2 hour job\".\n\n## What happened\n\nAGENTS.md says \"A minor/major cut does not start while any `P1` or `P2` issue is open\". During the v0.19.0 cut two such issues were filed after the release branch existed (issue 1417, P1, a red xtask unit test; issue 1398, P2, the Fanuc lathe live-tool feed cap). Fixing them in the cut means merging to main, merging main into the release branch and running the release gate again, about 50 minutes of gate and about two hours in all. The maintainer decided in the question dialog: \"Tag now as it is\"; both were named as known issues on the release PR.\n\n## What to change (AGENTS.md, \"Priorities\" and \"Commits and Releases\")\n\n- The `P1`/`P2` rule is a start condition: it is checked once, when the cut starts (step 1). The session records the time and the list of open `P1`/`P2` issues (none) in the release PR body.\n- A `P1` or `P2` issue filed after that moment does not restart the cut and is not merged into it. The cut finishes on the tree that passed the release gate. Each such issue is named under \"Known issues\" in the release notes on the GitHub release and in a comment on the release PR, and its fix merges after the tag and ships in the next minor.\n- The maintainer can still stop a cut by saying so; no agent stops or restarts one for a late issue. An agent that finds a late `P1` (unsafe or wrong output) tells the maintainer in one line and goes on.\n- Failures of the cut's own release gate are different: they are what the gate is for, and are still fixed in the cut as today.\n- Update the `merge-ready` skill's precondition text and the release steps where they repeat the rule.\n\nProcess files change: bump `.claude/PROCESS_VERSION`, add a `docs/decisions/` entry quoting the maintainer, announce on issue 681 when it merges.\n\nDone means: AGENTS.md states the start-condition reading and the known-issues step, the skills that repeat the rule agree with it, `PROCESS_VERSION` is bumped, and nothing in the text lets an agent restart a cut for an issue filed after its start.\n",
